WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.063
- [Nick Jonas] I brought you a gift.

00:00:01.063 --> 00:00:01.896
- First of all,

00:00:01.896 --> 00:00:04.160
you're invited anytime, you bring alcohol.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.670
So wait, what is this?

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.016
Villa wine?

00:00:07.016 --> 00:00:09.923
- So this is my new
tequila with John Varvatos.

00:00:09.923 --> 00:00:10.756
- [Kelly] Dang!

00:00:10.756 --> 00:00:11.589
- It started about two
and a half years ago.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:14.610
We started a process of
working with Stoli Group

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.913
to develop our own tequila
and wanna have some?

00:00:15.913 --> 00:00:18.030
- Um, can we try, I know
it's like, you know,

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.500
this show airs at like 9 AM,

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.921
I'm looking at your Nashville.
- Just a little bit.

00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:22.220
- But yeah, I don't wanna be rude.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.786
So let's do it, Nick, let's do it.

00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:24.670
(audience laughter)

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.550
- Congrats to you.
- My mamma raised a polite

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.050
young lady, so I will drink your tequila.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:30.950
- Sorry we don't have
enough for everybody, guys.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.003
- I mean, fine, I guess we're
rationing it, but it's fine.

00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:33.494
It's fine.

00:00:33.494 --> 00:00:34.327
(audience laughter)

00:00:34.327 --> 00:00:35.160
- Cheers.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:40.571
(audience whoops and applause)

00:00:40.571 --> 00:00:41.672
- That is good.
- Smooth, huh?

00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:42.538
- It's so smooth.

00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:43.960
I was a little nervous because
usually I do like a lime,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.400
I mean, I don't drink ever but, um.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.820
No, I do usually like salt and a lime.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.420
That's really smooth.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.253
- Yeah, we're excited about it.

00:00:50.253 --> 00:00:52.050
So we just launched this
one on the East Coast

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.360
and the rest of the
country's kinda starting now,

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.923
but then we have reposado and anejo

00:00:54.923 --> 00:00:56.370
as well that's coming out.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.510
- I'm into it, so, okay,
let's celebrate real quick.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:00.343
You want another one?

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:01.176
Okay, fine, I will.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.990
Let's celebrate and drink to
your first season of The Voice.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.167
You don't have to.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.014
(audience laughs)

00:01:07.014 --> 00:01:08.510
Be a better person than
me, I'm trying to be kind.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:09.570
I just want to celebrate the fact that

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.403
you're going to be on The Voice,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.712
and I'm going to kick your tail, oh!

00:01:11.712 --> 00:01:12.822
- That's not true.

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:14.497
(audience laughs)

00:01:14.497 --> 00:01:15.975
Incorrect.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.808
(audience cheers)

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.910
I'm not going to clap for that.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:22.743
- I'm not gonna clap for that.

00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:24.370
I refuse to clap for that, man.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.260
- It has been a good little

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.870
friendly competition so far though.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:27.810
- It has!

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.900
- We've, you know, we've done the blinds,

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.630
which has been really
fun, my first ever, uh,

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.060
assembled a good team.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:33.893
I feel confident about it.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:37.317
- Yes, and we like a lot
of the same sound, yes?

00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:38.197
- I didn't expect that.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.030
- I did.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.040
I thought John and I
would go head to head,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:40.873
but it's really you and I.

00:01:40.873 --> 00:01:42.180
- No, I knew it, I knew it.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.330
And they, the guys, were talking about it.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.517
I was like, "He's going to be...

00:01:44.517 --> 00:01:47.190
"I'm going to have to
battle Nick fricking Jonas."

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.046
(audience laughs)

00:01:48.046 --> 00:01:49.290
Like, what, I'm not going to win there.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.680
I'm like a mom, like, so
not cool compared to you.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.880
Like what?

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.230
So let's talk about it.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.370
I know people probably ask all the time,

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:57.040
but I love Priyanka, and you know this--

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:57.873
- Me too!

00:01:57.873 --> 00:02:00.314
She's so cool, but I didn't realize,

00:02:00.314 --> 00:02:02.670
well, not really, I didn't
realize, like, how fast...

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.380
Well, okay, what was your first date like,

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.213
first of all?

00:02:05.213 --> 00:02:06.992
- Well, it's kind of a long story.

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:07.825
- Okay.

00:02:07.825 --> 00:02:08.658
- But I'll, I'll, I'll tell it.

00:02:08.658 --> 00:02:09.491
- Synopsis.

00:02:09.491 --> 00:02:11.610
- So basically we, um, we
were told by a mutual friend

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.300
that we should meet and he
said, "I'll connect you guys."

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.490
He never did and I got impatient,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.210
so I direct messaged her on Twitter

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:19.043
- Get it!

00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:19.876
- And she responded.

00:02:19.876 --> 00:02:20.710
We talked on, you know,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.510
back and forth about a year on texts.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.960
And then we finally met in person,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.190
and it wasn't, it wasn't really a date,

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.820
we just met in person
and went for a drink.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.220
And then about a year later we went on

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.620
our first official date
to the Hollywood bowl

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.620
to go see the Beauty and the Beast Live.

00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:35.518
- That's adorable!

00:02:35.518 --> 00:02:36.730
- Uh, you know, just
recently we played there

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.470
to kind of end the first leg of the tour

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.140
and she sat two boxes away from where

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.527
we sat on her first
date, it was very cool.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.370
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.040
So what I didn't know
though was y'all got,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.940
y'all got married pretty quick.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.777
Like people, I heard people kept going,

00:02:47.777 --> 00:02:49.340
"Whoa, that's moving fast!"

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.020
First of all, stay in your lane.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:51.853
- [Nick[ Exactly!

00:02:51.853 --> 00:02:52.686
(audience laughs)

00:02:52.686 --> 00:02:53.594
Mind your own business.
- Okay!

00:02:53.594 --> 00:02:54.746
So mind yourself!

00:02:54.746 --> 00:02:56.177
- I think, you know,
when you know, you know,

00:02:56.177 --> 00:02:58.160
and we heard that pretty
much from everybody

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.320
once we told people we were engaged.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.610
Uh, but we don't, you know, it was,

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.920
it was kind of magical, you know,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.390
just within, uh, eight, nine weeks

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.440
we were, you know, talking about marriage

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.885
and within 10, 11 weeks we were engaged.

00:03:10.885 --> 00:03:11.718
- [Kelly] That's amazing!

00:03:11.718 --> 00:03:13.720
- And we got married
in December last year.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.620
So our one year's coming up on the first.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:16.650
- That's so exciting.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.520
Congratulations!

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.699
It's really very cool to find someone

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:21.346
you love like that to be your best friend.

00:03:21.346 --> 00:03:22.490
It's so cool.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.100
So I heard when I was doing the...

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.370
I was reading the pre-interview for this,

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.130
I had no idea that y'all
opened for me in 2005.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:29.963
- [Nick] Well we did.

00:03:29.963 --> 00:03:31.490
- Because I feel like
I just got really cool.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:34.160
- No, well so, no one
cared about us in 2005.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.970
We were just coming up and
basically to get other gigs,

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.550
we listed the other acts
that we'd 'opened up for',

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.620
but that really just meant that we were

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.190
on like the outside
stage in the parking lot

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.140
while you were playing for 40,000 people.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:46.997
- Still, still the same.

00:03:46.997 --> 00:03:48.546
- But you helped us get
a lot of gigs after that.

00:03:48.546 --> 00:03:49.379
- Oh my gosh!

00:03:49.379 --> 00:03:51.436
- So thank you, we owe you 20 percent.

00:03:51.436 --> 00:03:53.770
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.370
- So now you're on tour for real.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.280
So tell us about Happiness Begins.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.160
- Uh, yeah, so this has
been quite the crazy year

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:01.993
for the family.

00:04:01.993 --> 00:04:04.440
Um, you know, just a year ago right now

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.380
we had just started recording music,

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.400
uh, together again and, um, you know,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.490
looking a year later we're finishing up

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:14.810
the first leg of a crazy tour,

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.660
and, um, also the album,
you know, Happiness Begins.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.980
But it all started with a documentary,

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.320
which we call Chasing Happiness,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.900
which was kind of just to tell
our story of our childhood,

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.110
you know, our father was a pastor

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:28.390
and we had a pretty crazy
journey in the church

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.100
and then into our music career together.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.070
And we had really no intention

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:34.180
of getting the band back together.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.960
But after filming for a little while

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.320
and kind of healing some
of those family wounds

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.050
that were there from our
years of working together

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.270
in the past, we were able to look at this

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.140
with a fresh view and,
and really kind of all

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.860
in different ways find our happiness.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.660
And so we, we went for it

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.395
and it's been an unforgettable year.

00:04:50.395 --> 00:04:51.240
It's been really amazing.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.073
- That's really cool.

00:04:52.073 --> 00:04:53.920
Like, not only, I mean I get like the fans

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.050
are excited about it,
but it's way more cool

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:56.883
for you and your family.

00:04:56.883 --> 00:04:58.620
Like that's a hard thing to, like,

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.100
I mean, that's my road family over there

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.070
and it's, it's hard to all
be together all the time,

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:02.903
especially when you're related.

00:05:02.903 --> 00:05:03.870
I can't even imagine that.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.110
So that's really cool that this ended.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.800
- It's really special to
share that with family.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.150
- If the documentary,
would you release it if

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.430
y'all wouldn't have gotten together?

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.263
- I think so, yeah.

00:05:10.263 --> 00:05:12.480
I think, you know, we had
spent money making it,

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:13.361
so we probably...

00:05:13.361 --> 00:05:15.352
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:15.352 --> 00:05:16.185
- You're like, "Yep!"

00:05:16.185 --> 00:05:17.788
- And I think it was an
important story to tell,

00:05:17.788 --> 00:05:18.910
you know, and that was, kind of,

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.080
I think, the thing that
was, to us, so special

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.170
about it, is that there
was no intention to,

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.450
to come back and do this
again at the beginning.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.750
But when we actually just sat
down and did the hard work

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.220
that, you know, most families have to do,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.780
we all go through things
with the people we love,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.650
and, uh, whether it's
the family you choose

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.483
or it's your blood.

00:05:32.483 --> 00:05:33.316
- It's usually the ones
you love the most, yeah.

00:05:33.316 --> 00:05:34.260
- Yeah, you gotta go through it.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.020
And, and, um, and we did.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.270
And, you know, we look
up at the other side

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.930
and we're all kind of in
the best place in our lives.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.590
- I know, you're all
married now, like, yeah.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.185
- All married.

00:05:43.185 --> 00:05:44.730
Brother's got two kids
and it's a beautiful time.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.230
And to have been able to go through that

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:47.470
with your family is,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.150
is, I think we're all really grateful,

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.880
and aware of how unique it is,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.305
and so it's just been special.

00:05:52.305 --> 00:05:53.138
- So cool.

00:05:53.138 --> 00:05:54.630
I will say you have, like,

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.052
um, the most famous family ever.

00:05:57.052 --> 00:05:58.510
(laughs)

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:01.350
It's, like, looking at everyone
listed in your family tree,

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.751
I'm like, "Hey, well!"

00:06:02.751 --> 00:06:04.500
Those kids are going to be, like,

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.220
they're not going to know what normal is.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.830
- [Nick] They're going to have some

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.451
cool aunts and cool uncles.

00:06:09.451 --> 00:06:11.050
- It's amazing, y'all
should have, you shouldn't,

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.720
but you should have a reality show.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.590
I just want to see it.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.390
I want to watch the dynamic of

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.980
all those famous people in one family.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:18.849
That's insane.

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:19.682
- I think the band might break up again

00:06:19.682 --> 00:06:20.526
if we had a reality show.

00:06:20.526 --> 00:06:21.359
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:06:21.359 --> 00:06:23.060
- If cameras are there all
the time, no you won't.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.240
You have to be on point.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:27.050
Um, do you have a
favorite song on the tour?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.490
- Uh, I, I, I have a few that I love.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.360
It's like picking a favorite kid, I guess.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:32.193
I can't pick one.

00:06:32.193 --> 00:06:33.026
- There are different vibes.

00:06:33.026 --> 00:06:33.960
- They're so connected
to my songwriting too

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.080
that's hard to pick one.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.350
Um, but we actually have just come out

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.460
with a Christmas song,

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.830
which has been a dream of ours forever.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:40.663
- I love Christmas.

00:06:40.663 --> 00:06:41.650
- Me too, it's my favorite.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.760
- Wait, y'all don't
have a Christmas album?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.211
What's wrong with you

00:06:44.211 --> 00:06:45.810
- We did an album back
in the day with Disney.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.570
We did a few, just songs here and there,

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:50.240
but this is like our
first, kinda, real swing

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.220
at doing a Christmas song with
the same group of writers,

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.610
producers that we work
with the rest of our music.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.443
- Oh my gosh!

00:06:55.443 --> 00:06:56.276
Do a whole album.

00:06:56.276 --> 00:06:57.260
I love Christmas music.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.480
- As long as you come on and duet with us.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.377
- I will sing with you,
unless you're just joking.

00:07:01.377 --> 00:07:02.210
- You already sang with
John a couple of times.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.043
- I did sing with John.

00:07:03.043 --> 00:07:04.503
(Audience cheers)

00:07:04.503 --> 00:07:06.940
I love, I love Christmas music.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:07.773
I think it's so cool cause

00:07:07.773 --> 00:07:09.182
you can get away with like
that cheesy good feeling.

00:07:09.182 --> 00:07:10.580
- When do you start
playing Christmas music?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.420
- Um, I actually started in,
and my staff will tell you,

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:14.600
I actually started, like, uh,

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.750
two months ago 'cause I was
wrapping presents in Montana,

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.180
we've a ranch there, and I was
wrapping Christmas presents.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.730
- So two months ago, so like September?

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:21.563
- Yep.

00:07:21.563 --> 00:07:22.528
- [Nick] Wow!

00:07:22.528 --> 00:07:23.557
- Never too early.

00:07:23.557 --> 00:07:24.390
(audience laughs)

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.760
Because I was wrapping Christmas presents;

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.420
November, December, are really busy.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.275
So I was having to do
everything beforehand, and so--

00:07:29.275 --> 00:07:31.037
- You did say you were
wrapping Christmas presents

00:07:31.037 --> 00:07:31.988
months in advance.

00:07:31.988 --> 00:07:32.821
- I was wrapping presents, yes.

00:07:32.821 --> 00:07:33.654
- That's impressive.

00:07:33.654 --> 00:07:34.487
- I do that.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.090
- I start shopping three days before.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.796
